cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpticalTwin in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "OpticalTwin: a browser-based 3D viewer and editor for optical laboratory setups"
abstract: >-
  OpticalTwin is a shared, server-hosted web application for viewing, arranging,
  and discussing optical laboratory setups in 3D. Setups are stored as OpenUSD
  scenes (millimetre units, Z-up, optical axis along +X) and edited in the
  browser through a React Three Fiber client backed by a Python/Flask server.
  Its scope is layout and planning — component fit, spacing, and alignment —
  rather than optical physics simulation.
type: software
